NOTES — Anime Adventures Macro + Reze Hub Integration
=====================================================

SOURCE
- Original hub: https://github.com/Saharalay1/Anime-Adventures/blob/main/Macro
- Title shown: "Reze is fineeeee v2.2"
- ~12108 lines, pure client Lua, uses executor filesystem (writefile/readfile/isfolder/makefolder/listfiles)

CORE STRUCTURE
- Everything lives in table1
- table1.folder1 = "FEMBOY"  (root for songs + configs on executor FS)
- table1.maingui = ScreenGui
- table1.frame = main window Frame
- Tabs created with table1.createtab(name, position) → returns button, page (ScrollingFrame)
- Default open tab: Main (table1.mainpage)

IMPORTANT TABS
- Main          → table1.mainpage          (game-specific features go here)
- General       → table1.generall
- Teleport      → table1.teleportttttttt
- Velocity      → table1.velocityyyyyyyy
- ESP, Aimbot, Hitbox, Misc, Lighting, Music, Settings, UI Settings, About

MAINTOGGLE
Signature (modern):
  local main, changedEvent, [actionEvent], ...valueBoxes =
    table1.maintoggle(
      "Title",
      "Mode1", "Mode2", ...,
      scale,
      parentPage,
      animate,
      modeType,
      textboxCount,
      [actionCount]
    )

- Returns actionEvent only when actionflag is set (last numeric arg)
- state stored in table1.maintoggleState[main]
- Mode stored as attribute: main:GetAttribute("Mode") / :SetAttribute("Mode", n)
- Foldable via state.fold / state.folded
- table1.foldAllMaintoggles() collapses everything at end of script

ACTION BUTTONS
- Created when actionflag=1
- Example (WalkSpeed):
  table1.walkspeedtoggle, table1.walkspeedchanged, table1.walkspeedaction, table1.walkspeedvalue =
    table1.maintoggle("WalkSpeed", "On", 1, table1.generall, true, 0, 1, 1)
- actionEvent fires on press/release according to hold/press setting

CONFIG SYSTEM (Reze)
- Path: FEMBOY/configs/*.json on executor filesystem
- Completely separate from macro configs

MACRO SYSTEM
- Lives entirely under Main tab
- Temporary recording buffer: table1.recordedActions (in-memory only)
- Destroyed when client starts a new recording or leaves the game
- Permanent macros saved as JSON StringValues under Workspace.FEMBOY.macroconfigs
- Completely independent of FEMBOY/configs

MACRO API
- table1.startRecording() / table1.stopRecording() (toggled by one action button REC)
- table1.saveMacro(name)
- table1.loadMacro(name)
- table1.deleteMacro(name)
- table1.listMacros()
- table1.replayMacro(name or nil)
- table1.stopReplay()
- table1.clearTemporaryMacro()

RECORDING
- Hooks __namecall for FireServer / InvokeServer
- Only logs: spawn_unit, upgrade_unit_ingame, sell_unit_ingame, change_priority, use_active_attack, vote_start
- Ignores UnreliableRemoteEvent
- Stores exact args, wave number, timeOffset since wave start, unitId, moneyAtTime
- On spawn_unit: listens ChildAdded on Workspace._UNITS to stamp unitName

REPLAY
- wavebasedtime true → wait recorded timeOffset after wave start
- false → spam in order as soon as wave is current
- place / upgrade / sell → spam until return value == true
- use_active_attack → keep trying
- skipfailuresandmoveontothenextwave → abandon remaining actions of old wave
- autovotestart → auto InvokeServer vote_start at beginning of replay

SETTINGS (table1.macroSettings)
- failureretry, skipfailuresandmoveontothenextwave, wavebasedtime, autovotestart, startupdelay, spaminterval, maxspamattempts

UI ON MAIN TAB
- One action-button maintoggle: Record Macro (toggles start/stop)
- Info maintoggle (foldable)
- Macro name textbox + Save / Load / Delete / Replay / Stop Replay
- Settings toggles for wave based time, auto vote start, skip failures

PATHS
- Workspace._wave_num
- Workspace._UNITS
- ReplicatedStorage.endpoints.client_to_server.*
- Players.LocalPlayer.PlayerGui.spawn_units.Lives.Frame.Resource.Money.Text

REMINDERS
- Macro configs ≠ Reze configs
- No prints
- Leave all pre-existing comments untouched
- Action button only for record start/stop
- Everything macro-related parents to table1.mainpage
- Reuses table1.Players, table1.Workspace, table1.HttpService, table1.RunService, table1.player, table1.white, table1.font
